WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.528 --> 00:00:15.289
Six weeks passed while we worked hard.

2
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.152
We planted fruit trees at Falconhurst.

3
00:00:18.912 --> 00:00:20.394
After that we worked at Tentholm.

4
00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.576
I wanted to make it safe in case of emergency.

5
00:00:24.277 --> 00:00:28.100
First we planted a thick, prickly hedge that would protect us from wild animals.

6
00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.084
Then we mounted two cannons from the wreck on a hill above the bay.

7
00:00:32.948 --> 00:00:36.969
The boys were growing strong as I encouraged them to run, climb, and swim.

8
00:00:37.749 --> 00:00:42.171
For fun, I also taught them how to use a lasso, and Jack took his everywhere.

9
00:00:43.131 --> 00:00:45.852
But all this work and play was wearing out their clothes.

10
00:00:48.493 --> 00:00:52.374
Therefore I decided to pay another visit to the wreck to replenish our wardrobes.

11
00:00:53.254 --> 00:00:56.935
I also wanted to see how much longer the vessel was likely to hold together.

12
00:00:57.775 --> 00:00:59.496
Luckily there hadn't been a storm yet.

13
00:01:00.332 --> 00:01:02.814
The three older boys and I set off in the sailboat.

14
00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:05.115
"Come, boys," I said.

15
00:01:05.135 --> 00:01:08.037
"Don't leave behind a single item of the slightest value.

16
00:01:08.898 --> 00:01:10.719
Search the ship to the bottom of its hold."

17
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.541
The boys scattered throughout the ship.

18
00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:18.044
Soon everything from bales of cloth to window shutters lay in a heap on the deck.

19
00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.706
We loaded the sailboat and went onshore.

20
00:01:21.587 --> 00:01:23.708
After a few more trips, nothing remained.

21
00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:29.777
"I left two barrels of gunpowder on board and lit a very long fuse," I said to my

22
00:01:29.837 --> 00:01:31.438
wife when we returned to Tentholm.

23
00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:35.561
That night we ate supper at a spot from which we could see the wreck.

24
00:01:36.442 --> 00:01:39.804
Suddenly a vivid pillar of fire rose from the black waters.

25
00:01:39.824 --> 00:01:46.349
"That's the end of the brave ship that carried us from Switzerland," I said softly.

26
00:01:48.851 --> 00:01:52.854
We had planned the destruction of the ship, but we went to bed that night feeling sad.

27
00:01:53.794 --> 00:01:55.696
We felt as if we'd lost a dear friend.

28
00:01:56.992 --> 00:02:00.315
The next morning we found the shore lined with a rich supply of wood.

29
00:02:01.076 --> 00:02:02.997
Our ship had been good to us until the end.

30
00:02:04.539 --> 00:02:09.323
Meanwhile Fritz and I had been planning another expedition into the countryside surrounding Falconhurst.

31
00:02:09.343 --> 00:02:12.005
"Why does Fritz always get to go?"

32
00:02:12.325 --> 00:02:13.086
complained Jack.

33
00:02:13.106 --> 00:02:15.328
"Yes," said my wife.

34
00:02:15.348 --> 00:02:18.110
"I'd like to see what's beyond Falconhurst too."

35
00:02:20.652 --> 00:02:24.896
So the next morning the whole family started off in our cart pulled by the cow and donkey.

36
00:02:25.652 --> 00:02:28.613
We took everything necessary for an expedition of several days.

37
00:02:29.653 --> 00:02:34.454
On the first day we gathered more berries to make candles and tapped the rubber trees for their

38
00:02:34.515 --> 00:02:35.175
gummy sap.

39
00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:40.856
After pitching our tent, we were enjoying supper when our donkey, Grizzle, let out a loud bray.

40
00:02:40.876 --> 00:02:43.097
"What's wrong with him?"

41
00:02:43.477 --> 00:02:45.638
asked little Franz as the donkey galloped away.

42
00:02:45.658 --> 00:02:51.479
"I have no idea," I replied, "but we can't afford to lose such a valuable animal."

43
00:02:52.179 --> 00:02:56.398
We followed the donkey for a short distance, but had to give up because it was getting dark.

44
00:02:57.118 --> 00:02:59.280
The next morning I took Jack and the dogs with me.

45
00:03:00.021 --> 00:03:04.484
We followed Grizzle's tracks in the soil until they mingled with those of other animals.

46
00:03:05.425 --> 00:03:09.308
At last we reached a wide plain, and I saw a herd of large animals.

47
00:03:10.309 --> 00:03:15.433
Buffalo! Turk and Juno saw them too and dashed forward before I could stop them.

48
00:03:16.214 --> 00:03:19.937
The dogs surrounded a young buffalo, causing the rest of the herd to attack.

49
00:03:20.718 --> 00:03:23.240
I fired my gun in the air, and the herd retreated.

50
00:03:23.944 --> 00:03:28.206
"If we could capture that little buffalo, we might train him to work for us," I said.

51
00:03:28.226 --> 00:03:29.887
"I know what to do!"

52
00:03:30.207 --> 00:03:30.767
said Jack.

53
00:03:31.707 --> 00:03:36.069
He pulled out his lasso and, twirling it in the air, caught the buffalo by the hind legs.

54
00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.850
We fastened a rope around the buffalo's neck.

55
00:03:39.591 --> 00:03:43.853
With the dogs herding it from either side, we managed to get the buffalo to walk with us.

56
00:03:44.853 --> 00:03:48.034
I decided to give up our donkey search for the moment and return to camp.

57
00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.816
Juno dashed ahead and was about to rush into a little cave.

58
00:03:52.596 --> 00:03:54.918
Suddenly a large jackal sprang out at her.

59
00:03:55.638 --> 00:03:59.401
Turk joined the fight, and the two dogs managed to drive off the jackal.

60
00:04:00.922 --> 00:04:02.423
Jack peered inside the cave.

61
00:04:02.444 --> 00:04:04.165
"Baby jackals!

62
00:04:05.025 --> 00:04:06.607
Oh, Father, may I take one home?"

63
00:04:07.507 --> 00:04:08.808
I glanced around nervously.

64
00:04:08.828 --> 00:04:11.050
"Hurry up before the parents come back."

65
00:04:11.831 --> 00:04:15.333
Jack went into the cave and emerged with a yellow cub the size of a cat.

66
00:04:16.454 --> 00:04:18.776
He was eager to show his new pet to his brothers.

67
00:04:19.612 --> 00:04:21.013
"Look what I found!"

68
00:04:21.333 --> 00:04:23.935
he said triumphantly when we arrived back at our tent.

69
00:04:24.635 --> 00:04:25.716
"And look what I found!"

70
00:04:25.976 --> 00:04:28.157
said Fritz, showing us a small eagle.

71
00:04:28.177 --> 00:04:30.298
"Now, boys," I said.

72
00:04:30.318 --> 00:04:31.919
"You're collecting a lot of pets.

73
00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.881
It's not your mother's job to take care of them.

74
00:04:35.561 --> 00:04:40.944
You must each look after your own, and if I find any animal neglected, I will set it

75
00:04:41.004 --> 00:04:42.505
free. Do you understand?"

76
00:04:43.346 --> 00:04:46.287
The boys nodded solemnly while my wife looked quite relieved.
